# HTML tags

## Line breaks

  First line
  second line
  third line
  fourth line
  fifth.

## Keys and marks

  Press `Ctrl`+`C` to copy, or `Page Down` to
  move on.

  Some text is marked as found, even in bold.

  A <kbd>key that never closes stays as
  source.

## Scripts: x² and H₂O

  Water is H₂O, x² + y² = rⁿ⁺¹ on the 2ⁿᵈ try,
  and xᵃⁱ keeps one size. Unicode has no
  script characters for π or for code, so eiπ
  and a`b` have none.

## Details

  ▼ A summary with `Esc`

  The content is Markdown, as GitHub shows it:

  - one
  - two

  ▼ Written on one line

  The content & its tags are plain text.

  ▼ Details

  Without a summary, the block is called
  Details.

  - A list item

    ▼ Inside a list

    Content in the list.

  > ▼ Inside a quote
  >
  > Content in the quote.

  ▼ Outer, no blank line before the inner

  ▼ Inner

  Content of the inner one.

  Content of the outer one.

  ▼ With an HTML paragraph

  The paragraph's text, read as plain text.

  ▼ Text right after the end

  Content.

  Text after the details, in the same HTML
  block.

## Bold, italic and code

  Some bold and strong text, italic and
  emphasis, struck and deleted, and `code
  with  spaces` in running text.

  Nested bold italic, and Markdown around
  HTML.

  A lone <b>bold never closes and a
  <b>mismatched</strong> pair stays as source,
  as do the tags of <code>code with bold
  inside</code>.

  ▼ A bold and `code` summary

  Body of the details.

## Entities

  ▼ Fish & chips — 5 € &foo;

  One line — © … &mdash; &Mdash;

## Headings

### An HTML heading

#### With an `align`, drawn left-aligned

## The `kiri` — tool

  <h7>No such heading stays as source</h7>

## Other tags

  Text with <span>a span</span> and <u>an
  underline</u> stays as source.

  <div>
  A div block stays as source.
  </div>

  ▼ Never closed

  Runs to the end of the document.
